## Saved session contexts (/context-save) are always tracked.
## Topic folders are human-named and WILL collide with the build-output patterns above —
## `Distribution/Release/` was silently swallowed by `[Rr]elease/`. Re-include the whole tree so
## a topic name can never make a saved context disappear without a word.
!.claude/contexts/**

## Scratch output from rehearsing an example (see examples/*/RUNBOOK.md)
examples/**/.work/

## Agent worktrees. A subagent given `isolation: "worktree"` gets a throwaway checkout here; the BRANCH
## it commits to is a normal ref in the repo, so nothing is lost when the directory goes. Ignored because
## the checkout is scratch, and because a stray one left behind by an interrupted agent should never look
## like uncommitted work.
.claude/worktrees/

# Guardrails per-run runtime state inside a committed plan folder (rewritten every run;
# `--fresh` clears it). The plan DEFINITION, the review marker and the review reports under
# state/reviews/ are committed; run.json, state.json and logs/ are not.
docs/plans/*/state/run.json
docs/plans/*/state/state.json
docs/plans/*/state/merge-conflicts.log
docs/plans/*/logs/
docs/plans/*/captured/
